diff -rupN jq.py-1.12.0-orig/README.rst jq.py-1.12.0/README.rst
--- jq.py-1.12.0-orig/README.rst	2026-07-10 10:45:56.000000000 +0000
+++ jq.py-1.12.0/README.rst	2026-08-28 15:00:43.553848193 +0000
@@ -186,6 +186,29 @@ Calling ``compile()`` with the ``args``
     program = jq.compile("$a + $b + .", args={"a": 100, "b": 20})
     assert program.input_value(3).first() == 123
 
+Library Search Path
+~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+
+Calling ``compile()`` or any other method that accepts a jq script
+with the ``library_paths`` argument configures the path jq will use in
+searching for files when processing the ``import`` and ``include``
+statements.
+
+The argument must be an array of strings, each naming a path to be
+searched with home directories as `Python's os.path.expanduser()
+<https://docs.python.org/3/library/os.path.html#os.path.expanduser>`_
+would expand them.
+
+If not provided, the search path is that described in the `Modules
+<https://jqlang.org/manual/#modules>`_ section of the jq manual.
+
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+    program = jq.compile('import "siconvert" as si; si::as_integer(.)', library_paths=["/usr/lib/jqstuff"])
+    assert program.input_value("1234K").first() == 1234000
+
+
 Convenience functions
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
 
